# leads: forming and trimming at the bench (decision C15). The DIP in
# the vise; the arm brings the resistor's lead 1 to pin 3, 2.5 mm down
# the pin, and pincer P1 holds it there; the iron station solders the
# joint; the cutter station S4 trims the pin's excess 1 mm past the
# joint; pincer P2 bends
# the resistor's other lead down, round a mandrel 3 mm from its body,
# toward where its next part will be; the turntable presents that lead
# to the cutter station S4, which trims it to 8 mm -- the rest falls
# into the bin; P1 lets go and the resistor stays, soldered on.
reset circuit=demo
tool A tweezers
pick A U1 grasp=ends
place A U1 at=0,0,-24 rpy=0,0,90
vise close
release A U1
pick A R1 grasp=body
lift A mm=80
move A to=0,60,60 rpy=180,0,90
move A to=34.81,1.27,-14.05
align A R1.1.tip to=U1.3.2.5 gap=0.1
pinch P1 on=R1.1 at=6
release A R1
lift A mm=60
present U1.3+R1.1 at=S1
touch S1 at=U1.3+R1.1 dwell=2
feed S1 mm=2 rate=1
back S1
wait until=U1.3+R1.1 below=100
present U1.3.3.5 at=S4
trim S4 on=U1.3 at=3.5
bend P2 on=R1.2 at=3 angle=90 toward=0,0,-1
present R1.2.8 at=S4
trim S4 on=R1.2 at=8
unpinch P1
